# Episode 3 — optional judge backends.
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill real values locally.
# NEVER commit `.env` (it is gitignored).
#
# With no keys set, demo_ep3.py uses the offline keyword heuristic.
# Jev wiring guide: docs/JEV_SETUP.md

# --- Jev / TypeSafe (prefer when you have early access) ---
# You need BOTH a key AND a base URL. Key alone will not invent Jev results.
# Use either JEV_API_KEY or TYPESAFE_API_KEY (first non-empty wins: JEV then TYPESAFE).
# JEV_API_BASE = host + version prefix ONLY — do NOT append /judge
#   (code POSTs to `{JEV_API_BASE}/judge`). Confirm the real base from TypeSafe docs/dashboard.
# JEV_API_KEY=
# TYPESAFE_API_KEY=
# JEV_API_BASE=https://YOUR-REAL-BASE-FROM-TYPESAFE

# --- LLM JSON fallback (used if Jev unavailable) ---
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-3-5-haiku-latest

# --- Optional: force a backend for demos ---
# jev | openai | anthropic | heuristic
# JUDGE_BACKEND=
